---
title: Country Loaf
cooklang: 2
servings: 8
makes: 1 loaf
unit system: metric
time:
  prep: 40 minutes
  total: 3 hours 30 minutes
choices:
  leavening:
    same-day: Instant yeast, bake this afternoon
    sourdough:
      description: Levain, bake tomorrow morning
      time:
        prep: 50 minutes
        total: 27 hours
techniques: [knead, stretch and fold, prove, bake]
tags: [bread, baking]
---

= Levain ?sourdough ~{-1%day} -> levain

`Mix` @active starter{20%g}, @&bread flour{50%g} and @&water{50%g} in a #jar{}. Leave at
room temperature for ~prove{8-10%hours} until ~{bubbly and domed}.

= Dough -> dough

`Mix` @bread flour{500%g}|{450%g}?sourdough, @water{350%g}|{300%g}?sourdough and
@fine salt{10%g} in a #large bowl{}.

?same-day: `Add` @instant yeast{7%g} and knead for ~{10%minutes}.

?sourdough: `Add` @&levain{} and squeeze it through the dough until ~{even}.

?same-day: `Prove covered` covered for ~prove{1%hour} until ~{doubled}.

?sourdough: `Stretch and fold` the @&dough{} every 30 minutes for ~prove{4%hours}.

= Shape and bake

`Shape` into a tight round and set seam-side up in a floured #banneton{}.

?same-day: `Prove` for ~prove{45%minutes}.

?sourdough: `Retard` in the #fridge{} for ~chill{12-14%hours}.

`Bake 240 °C covered` in a preheated #dutch oven{} at 240 °C, lid on for ~oven{20%minutes}, then `bake uncovered` for
~oven{20-25%minutes}. `Cool` on a #wire rack{} for ~rest{1%hour}.
